    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that when an owner is created, the response (and subsequent reads) include a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` derived from the stored names.\n\nSince owner responses on every endpoint (`POST /api/owners`, `GET /api/owners/{id}`, etc.) all flow through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, I implemented it there so the derived field is consistent across all reads. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored entity names.\n\nThe acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
